{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages","id":403822,"title":"Share your custom Lineages!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-12T16:20:30-08:00","id":403822,"title":"Share your custom Lineages!","content":"Seeing the Hollow in Dark Eras and having the knowledge that Extempore will be in 2e, I'm powerfully curious about Lineages beyond the core five. What have you folks come up with?<br /> <br /> I'm considering a volcanic Lineage that began with an Extempore on some Pacific island (drawing on both Tammuz and Frankenstein mechanics), and considering an Ulgan variant that draws more heavily on the Orphean possibility, as I think ghosts are more in-theme for Promethean than animist spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T02:21:19-08:00","id":404331,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to write these up completely because I have them for submission pieces, but as I've mentioned them before online I'll just mention at my own table the &quot;Belenus&quot; (Wickermen) were the Fire/Choleric Lineage that died out before Victor's experiment. And of course, one shouldn't forget the &quot;Moreau&quot;, made from the grafted bodies of still living animals into humanoid shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T02:30:26-08:00","id":404335,"title":"","content":"I was working on an infernal linage called the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/54098-baalim-an-infernal-lineage\">Baalim</a>. It reminds me I should complete them sometime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T12:48:21-08:00","id":409234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=404331#post404331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to write these up completely because I have them for submission pieces, but as I've mentioned them before online I'll just mention at my own table the &quot;Belenus&quot; (Wickermen) were the Fire/Choleric Lineage that died out before Victor's experiment. And of course, one shouldn't forget the &quot;Moreau&quot;, made from the grafted bodies of still living animals into humanoid shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Moreau basically a biological counterpart to the Unfleshed, to basically see how far you can stretch the Divine Fire and still make a potential person? I think I'm in love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:42:49-08:00","id":409861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=404331#post404331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to write these up completely because I have them for submission pieces, but as I've mentioned them before online I'll just mention at my own table the &quot;Belenus&quot; (Wickermen) were the Fire/Choleric Lineage that died out before Victor's experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the idea of this bunch being the actual Fire lineage while the Wretched are an Electricity one (although I also give the Wretched a different origin from Victor Frankenstein).<br /> <br /> I'm going to wait for the second edition before I write these up more fully, but I have the:<br /> <br /> Dumuz: (Yes, this is a different transliteration of Tammuz; this is because the means of creating the Tammuz golems were derived from those of the Dumuz, who were the real embodiments of the Inanna backstory). As the results of an attempt to resurrect a loved one, they feel - and maybe have - a stronger connection to their bodies' former owners. Their Disquiet and Torment are elegiac, centred around mourning and feelings of loss; people have a tendency to see their loved ones reflected in the Dumuz and become angry when the reflection doesn't persist.<br /> <br /> Delphine: Derived from the Oracle of Delphi; their origin myth claims that their progenitor called the Fire into her own flesh and became a Promethean, though that's not carried over to the creation of any today. Anyhow, they're oracles, creatures of ecstatic visions, and connected to both the Sun and underground places. Their Disquiet provokes alternating certainties and confusions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T04:01:33-08:00","id":409873,"title":"","content":"I've created a lineage something like a year ago; its members are, amusingly enough, also called &quot;Hollow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basic idea:<br /> <br /> Some guy (his name isn't important, appropriately so for the Hollow, as you'll find out later) gets it into his head that his deceased wife can be brought back from the dead. He wants to reanimate her body.<br /> <br /> What makes him different from other potential progenitors is that he empathically doesn't want to create *new* life - he wants his wife back.<br /> <br /> So he creates an appropriate altar for the ritual of resurrection - ornating it with objects dear to his wife, that are supposed to bring her spirit closer to the world of the living. He cuts up the corpse. He puts it back together. He starts to pray.<br /> <br /> His obsession is sufficient to draw the attention of the Principle and force the Pyros into this corpse. And the corpse of his wife opens her eyes.<br /> <br /> This woman isn't his wife, though. She doesn't even always look like her. Sometimes her personality changes. Sometimes her physical features change. She's not a person. She's nobody.<br /> <br /> It breaks his heart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The quintessential idea of the Hollow is this: all Promethean, upon their creation, are new persons, without personality or memories. With the Hollow, this idea is drawn to its logical conclusion - in trying to bring someone back from the dead with her personality intact, the man achieved just the opposite - the resulting creature has even less personality and individuality than the average Promethean. The Hollow are social and physical chameleons - they have the means to be anyone they want. Which doesn't give them any personality of their own. Their Pilgrimage involves finding a way to be somebody - as opposed to nobody.<br /> <br /> Humor: Void. The Hollow's Pyros doesn't have distinctive traits or humor of its own.<br /> <br /> Bestowment: 9 again on rolls involving Subterfuge, disguise and pretending to be someone else. Failed rolls can be rerolled.<br /> <br /> Many Hollow eventually learn Deception Transmutations.<br /> <br /> Disquiet: People ignore the Hollow and do not acknowledge his existence. Sometimes people also refuse to trust the Hollow. Sometimes they try to manipulate him, attempting to force a change in his behaviour, outlook and personality.<br /> <br /> Disfigurement: When using Pyros, the Hollow appears to have no physical features and face at all.<br /> <br /> The Torment of the Hollow is that while those around them are rapidly losing identity, the Hollow is picking those traits up, searching for something, anything that will make them more real, more a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:50:37-08:00","id":416227,"title":"","content":"I created a lineage based on Homunculus myth called the &quot;Homuncio&quot; but I don't think it was very well received...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T19:59:08-07:00","id":529548,"title":"","content":"I'm entertaining the idea of creating a Lineage similar to the Galateids. They'll be ceramic dolls made with human ashes mixed in with the clay. Not sure which humor (probably blood given the effects of Disquiet) or what kind of bestowment. Their Disquiet will be weird. Most people will not feel it as hard, but children will. Kids will actually want to play with the Promethean! Eventually they will want the Promethean all to themselves though, and start getting violent with other kids who also want to play. Parents of the children under effect of Disquiet become fearful for their kids, and then make their Disquiet rolls at some kind of penalty.<br /> <br /> There aren't any myths or folklore that lend themselves to something like this, are there? That's one of the big stumbling blocks, right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T06:33:36-07:00","id":529865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=404331#post404331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to write these up completely because I have them for submission pieces, but as I've mentioned them before online I'll just mention at my own table the &quot;Belenus&quot; (Wickermen) were the Fire/Choleric Lineage that died out before Victor's experiment. And of course, one shouldn't forget the &quot;Moreau&quot;, made from the grafted bodies of still living animals into humanoid shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember those! I used to post on the pre-Onyx Path forums, under a different name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T06:39:59-07:00","id":529869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lackey Man Ren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=529548#post529548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm entertaining the idea of creating a Lineage similar to the Galateids. They'll be ceramic dolls made with human ashes mixed in with the clay. Not sure which humor (probably blood given the effects of Disquiet) or what kind of bestowment. Their Disquiet will be weird. Most people will not feel it as hard, but children will. Kids will actually want to play with the Promethean! Eventually they will want the Promethean all to themselves though, and start getting violent with other kids who also want to play. Parents of the children under effect of Disquiet become fearful for their kids, and then make their Disquiet rolls at some kind of penalty.<br /> <br /> There aren't any myths or folklore that lend themselves to something like this, are there? That's one of the big stumbling blocks, right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am immediately reminded off a novel I read about a year ago, <i>Doll Bones</i>, by Holly Black. More of a ghost story, by an author best known for work well suited to Changeling. (Both Lost and Dreaming.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:47:41-07:00","id":532609,"title":"","content":"Not mine, I take no credit. but pretty cool IMHO: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/116LMdtMWBsdZwyaCHquaPa0_qVjmVtQFBMDEGgyo9NQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:00:28-07:00","id":532615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=532609#post532609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not mine, I take no credit. but pretty cool IMHO: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/116LMdtMWBsdZwyaCHquaPa0_qVjmVtQFBMDEGgyo9NQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hey. Glad you like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:14:06-07:00","id":532622,"title":"","content":"I'm all for creating new stuff, and getting multiple players talking about similar ideas to talk to each other. Sharing is good. I also linked your work in the Pinocchio Lineage thread. Hope you don't mind.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:48:41-07:00","id":562490,"title":"","content":"Lineages made by <b>Major</b> templates take on traits of that template, right? So what about lineages made by <b>Minor</b> templates, like Psychics? I also have this horrible idea of a Promethean created by a researcher from The Chiron Group, whose body is mostly <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thaumatechnolgy implants...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:44:43-07:00","id":562553,"title":"","content":"Well it's not so much that major templates imbue their prometheans with their traits, rather that the creation rituals they use often reflect their own natures. <br /> <br /> So if you want a psychic created lineage, you'd have to figure out how their nature could be reflected in the creation ritual. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the promethean has a patchwork brain, maybe they're given life in a tub of cerebral spinal fluid charged with electricity, maybe their bones are replaced with conductive metals to enhance the nervous system, things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T21:09:53-07:00","id":562602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=562553#post562553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it's not so much that major templates imbue their prometheans with their traits, rather that the creation rituals they use often reflect their own natures.<br /> <br /> So if you want a psychic created lineage, you'd have to figure out how their nature could be reflected in the creation ritual.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the promethean has a patchwork brain, maybe they're given life in a tub of cerebral spinal fluid charged with electricity, maybe their bones are replaced with conductive metals to enhance the nervous system, things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas. I'll have to think about this some more...<br /> <br /> Here's another lineage from Malonkey1:<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/116LMdtMWBsdZwyaCHquaPa0_qVjmVtQFBMDEGgyo9NQ/edit#bookmark=id.y0qt2a68b2k9\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...d.y0qt2a68b2k9</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:00:05-07:00","id":615933,"title":"","content":"Has anyone considered a Lineage created by one of the Fallen? CWoD Demons would make interesting Demiurges...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T07:03:41-08:00","id":828201,"title":"","content":"I've though in the oriental paradigm with other set of elements (earth, fire, metal, water and wood). Perhaps in the Far East it could exist Lineages based on wood and metal, diferents of the occidental Prometeans.<br /> <br /> I think in some type of creature as the Swamp Thing or an Cyborg (perhaps a modern japanese corporation has created a Prometean based in the metal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T06:55:05-08:00","id":828760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=828201#post828201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've though in the oriental paradigm with other set of elements (earth, fire, metal, water and wood). Perhaps in the Far East it could exist Lineages based on wood and metal, diferents of the occidental Prometeans.<br /> <br /> I think in some type of creature as the Swamp Thing or an Cyborg (perhaps a modern japanese corporation has created a Prometean based in the metal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, looking them up on a horoscope site, I got:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Wood:</b><br /> It is yang/masculine in character. The predominant attributes are considered to be strength and flexibility, as with bamboo. It is also associated with qualities of generosity and idealism. One quality of the Wood element is leadership. It is the leader within us, that can take charge and determine a plan of action. The wood is one that seeks always to grow and expand. Wood heralds the beginning of life, springtime and buds, sensuality and fecundity.<br /> Wood type people are often aggressive or assertive, direct, and can have a strong temper and a lot of drive. They are usually outgoing and socially conscious and can be insensitive. The Wood element is associated with negative feelings of anger, and positive feelings of patience and altruism. </div> </div> </div>and<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Metal:</b><br /> Metal is yin/feminine in character, its motion is inwards and its energy is contracting. Metal represents the minerals, crystals, and gems of the world. The metal aspect is the diamond found within each one of us. It is similar to the Air Element found in western paradigms. The Metal Element is the breath of life. When you are connected to that experience, you know your own self-worth. You respect others and yourself; you are willing to give and receive acknowledgment for the magnificent being that you are. The qualities associated with metal are unyieldingness, rigidity, persistence, strength and determination. Metal type people like minimalism. They are organized, clean, and contained. They can be controlling, ambitious, forceful and set in their ways as metal is very strong; and they are self-reliant and prefer to handle their problems alone. The negative emotion associated with metal is grief, while the positive emotion is courage. </div> </div> </div>So a Wood Lineage could derive from a turbulent time in Chinese history - the Warring States, perhaps? - and an occult order (a change from a lone demiurge) trying to create inspiring figures to unite the Middle Kingdom. Obviously, a Promethean is no good for that, but that's how the Lineage could begin. By nature, their element drives them to be extroverted, and to push against the edges of humanity - though they also try to forge ties with other Prometheans and push them along their paths - they're especially drawn to Aurum and Aes Refinements. Their Torment might be a frenzy of activity - directed towards a purpose, but ill-thought out and counter productive. Their Disquiet might be a sense of pressure - people feel crowded and demanded-upon by the Promethean's presence. Their Wasteland could be marked by plentiful but unhealthy growth of plant life, and a sense that things are happening just out of sight.<br /> <br /> A Metal Lineage may be about treasure. While some of the Lineages have centred on resurrecting someone, a Metal Lineage may have begun with the goal of <i>enhancing</i> them. Prometheans of this Lineage retain that drive, and see a kind of perfection in themselves - but always with one crippling flaw. They're often drawn to Ferrum, Cuprum, and Cobalum, but are disproportionately likely to go Centimani. Disquiet could cause a kind of envy and sense of inadequacy in the face of the contained and controlled Promethean. Their Wasteland could either be rusty and decaying or very cold and sterile. Their Torment could be an extreme stubbornness.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T13:03:35-08:00","id":828927,"title":"","content":"Really good point. And another font of inspiration: The mithical Mandrake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Book_cover_%22Alraune%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune\" target=\"_blank\"> Alraune - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In this novel, a german doctor creates an artificial female basing in the medieval myth of the mandrake: the result is an insensible and perverse woman with attracs the fortune to his creator but inevitably causes the ruin around her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T07:10:54-08:00","id":830214,"title":"","content":"I actually wrote up a new Promethean line for the crossover game I'm running. I wanted an antagonist who wasn't out and out evil but still screwed with reality enough to give every splat a reason to care. <br /> <br /> The Mender was originally a mage who died in surprisingly mundane circumstances. His wife stumbled on strange things while going through his belongings...grimoires, arcane symbols, notes on impossible things, things with ink that crawled and writhed. She understood none of it but knew it was power. She made up her own shorthand of the symbols, took notes from her own limited understanding, assumed things that were patently wrong and from what little pop-culture magic she knew. She recognized the power, but didn't know how to use it and furthermore didn't care. Body parts came from other dead mages, found by recognizing symbols and learning signs. Her makeshift ritual worked...sort of. <br /> <br /> Supernal Magic apparently doesn't mix well with the Divine Fire. <br /> <br /> From the wreckage of the building stepped forth the unfortunate progenitor of a new lineage (whose name I havent figured out yet). <br /> <br /> To prevent this being a lonnnnnng post, I'll condense the necessary bits. <br /> <br /> Disfigurements: The Mender is twitchy and looking at him too long gives people a headache. When his disfigurements are revealed, the reason is obvious. His twitchiness turns into something reminiscent of slow-frame filming. Parts of his body phase in and out, flickering between representations of Supernal planes of existence. In one viewing, an observer could be assaulted by visions of the Mender's bones and decay from Stygia or see bestial fur from the Primal Wild's from wrist to shoulder alone. When they move, afterimages are left, different versions of his body moving out of synch with one another. <br /> <br /> Wasteland: Staying in one place too long, the Mender's presence starts to break down causality and normal laws of reality. Initially, its small things like disproportionately bad luck or things not bouncing in the direction physics would predict. Then matches start flaring into fireballs when struck and supernatural powers fizzle out or go wild. Visions similar to the disfigurements flicker over normal objects. FInally, the world seems to fall apart, despite the opposite happening: the Supernal realms are being drawn down simultaneously but separately. A tree is suddenly at the same time a skeletal dead thing and a wild dryad while the spirit of the tree writhes in angry confusion. It's as if we'd been wearing red-and-blue 3d glasses all our lives and someone suddenly took them away. <br /> <br /> Disquiet: I actually borrowed this from one of the Mage antagonist books: the Mender's disquiet resembles the False Awakening. On the plus side, it affects slightly fewer people more slowly than most other lineage's disquiet, but the effects are disastrous. Those affected have a sudden revelation and Awaken into great and terrible power. They believe they have become Extempore on the Path of Pyros, the Watchtower of the Divine Fire. As their powers grow exponentially, they see flickers of the Mender, even if he has passed on, offering escape and greater power and freedom. They become compelled to enact a ritual to PHYSICALLY ascend into their Watchtower which is, sadly, patently impossible. The resulting explosion and firestorm wreaks havoc and leaves echoes in every realm, and the local Twilight and Underworlds and even the Hedge feel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2706-comicjunkie1","name":"comicjunkie1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:11:32-07:00","id":848743,"title":"","content":"Got sick of the Transhuman thread being top of the page (I know, I was last person to post in it; that just makes me even more so).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I thought of a Lineage called the <b>Flayed</b>; I won't try to write them up properly until the second edition comes out, but this is what I brainstormed:<br /> <br /> More than one Lineage has begun with the attempt to resurrect someone - in this case, a man sacrificed at an Aztec temple long before the Europeans came. Why the priest chose to attempt this is a matter of conflicting legend: more modern Prometheans, living in a Christian milieu, suggest he was a young priest wracked with guilt; others say he was a friend or lover of the dead man, or that he was a sorcerer with darker uses for a body brought back from Mictlan. Regardless, he stitched the sacrifice back together, replaced the parts that were lost, and called upon the Sun to grant new life. The answer came from something else, but something just as bright.<br /> <br /> The Flayed are most &quot;common&quot; in Mexico, Central America, and the Southern US. Their generative act requires mutilating a body in a manner consistent with Aztec sacrifices, though fortunately, they can use one that's already dead (note that this is just the motions needed to make a new Promethean - none of them practice Aztec religion in any meaningful sense these days). A new Flayed can be made mostly from a single body, though the heart must come from another. While I'm calling them &quot;Flayed&quot; for now, their Disfigurement is actually that they look half-eaten. Their Humour is Sanguine, though their Element is characterised as Wind rather than Air.<br /> <br /> Many Flayed come into the world with a sense of purpose - the idea of some concrete &quot;quest&quot; they must complete as part of their Pilgrimmage. In modern times, those who feel this usually associate it with the person who provided their heart, and believe they must complete some business on this individual's behalf to set their ghost to rest (whether this is true or just a superstition is a question to be left unanswered).<br /> <br /> The Lineage began with the profaning of the body of a holy sacrifice, and this is reflected in their Disquiet and Torment. Those affected by Disquiet feel guilty and judged and resentful, and lash out at the Promethean for making them feel that way (and tend to be self-destructive as well). Flayed suffering Torment become antinomian, transgressing against every barrier they can - or maybe they should become bloody, revelling in spilled blood, excised hearts, and eaten flesh (basically, the surface violence of the old sacrifices, without the organised ritual or deeper spiritual meaning) - I'm not sure yet. I'm also not sure what their Wasteland should be, except that air and water should both have a rusty (aka bloody) tang.<br /> <br /> <br /> And inspired by the slasher demiurge thread, the <b>Untimely:</b><br /> <br /> The Untimely were also an attempt at resurrection. Someone whose family had been murdered desired revenge, an obsession that might have made them an Avenger slasher, but took a different course. Instead of using their loss to fuel their revenge, they meant to bring their family back to exact <i>their</i> revenge for <i>their</i> loss. Thus the Lineage has more than one Progenitor (or else the demiurge only managed to make a Promethean from one of them). It would also likely be a very young Lineage - a PC might easily be the first.<br /> <br /> Untimely must be made from the body of someone who's been murdered - less difficult than it might sound at first, given that the maker can murder someone herself - though this is considered the lazy option (and may be dangerous too; see below). Their humour is similar to melancholy, but with more of a deathly tinge - I'm unsure whether to call it Morbid or Elegiac. Their element is metal, the substance of which weapons are usually made. Their disfigurements are subtle: just an exaggerated version of their death wounds, constantly leaking blood and other fluids (though this doesn't harm the Promethean, it does normally mean the wound is visible even through clothing).<br /> <br /> All Untimely must grapple with the question of how to relate to the murder of their body's former owner - some decide on their answer very quickly, others may take many years. There's no right answer either: one might decide she must avenge it, another might decide it has little to do with her, a third might even look for a way to reward the killer for the act that enabled her existence (the first of these options is why a Promethean is often wary of killing someone to make offspring).<br /> <br /> Untimely Disquiet is direct: the affected begins to fantasise about killing the Promethean. Because they're unlikely to be a murderer at heart, they'll try to rationalise those feelings as being something else, but will still start following and stalking the Promethean nonetheless. Torment is about revenge: the Promethean will reflexively strike back against slights, her own or those of others, she won't care. [Functionally, Disquiet and Torment put those affected onto the edge of being slashers] The Wasteland corrodes and tarnishes metal, and nothing ever seems to get clean (bloodstains especially linger).<br /> <br /> <br /> And a bit more about the two I posted earlier...<br /> <br /> Many <b>Dumuz</b> believe they are an older version of the Tammuz (not all Tammuz disagree either, though some consider the Dumuz the younger Lineage, warped in the image of the Inanna legend, which had become attached to the Tammuz some time after their creation); others believe the two aren't related by anything but the coincidence of sharing an Element (some Tammuz who hold this view trace their own origin to the Golem of Prague, though tellings vary about whether their Progenitor was truly made from clay, or from the bodies of Jews who had been murdered by Gentiles - such a desecration of the dead would explain a lot about Prometheans).<br /> <br /> Regardless of origin, Dumuz must be made from the body of a single person - the generative act requires it be but into eight pieces (thus seven cuts, representing the seven gates of the Dark House), and covered with a mixture of earth from a grave and a grainfield. Their disfigurement makes them look skeletal, crusted with dirt and mud, and rimed with grave mold - witnesses may mistake them for some sort of zombie, though those who have encountered actual zombies will realise the Dumuz is something else.<br /> <br /> Many Dumuz believe that their soul already exists, and the Pilgrimmage is about finding it rather than creating it - this is likened to the Descent into the Underworld. [Whatever the 2nd Edition Osirians get that lets them visit the Underworld multiple times, if it's different from Revivication, the Dumuz should probably get it too]<br /> <br /> A Dumuz's Disquiet is elegiac: she prompts thoughts of the affected's loved ones; the affected see these people reflected in her, and get disappointed and angry when she doesn't live up to them. Her Torment is still: she becomes inert and finds it almost impossible to rouse herself to any action at all, which may even apply to self-defence; as if she were dead, in other words. The Wasteland resembles that of the Tammuz.<br /> <br /> The <b>Delphine</b> believe they descend from an Oracle of Delphi (one from before the period described in the great myths). Most of them believe that their demiurge and Progenitor were the same woman - that she called the Divine Fire into her own flesh to better understand the mysteries between death, life, and divinity - whether she thought it was worth it is lost to time, but those who pay too much attention to prophecy tend to suffer for it, so probably not.<br /> <br /> The generative act of the Delphine must be performed during daytime - the body must be brought out from an underground place and into the light of the Sun - this respect to Apollo is more important than the specific treatments used to raise the body. Delphine disfigurements are more unearthly than most Prometheans' - their bodies seem to darken almost to shadow, and appear wreathed in gas and vapour - witnesses tend to be left with a headache. Their Element is Vapour, and their Humour Ecstatic (there's some debate on whether these are actually different from Air and Sanguine, or if the Delphine are simply trying to distinguish themselves from the Galateid).<br /> <br /> I can't recall off the top of my head whether 2nd Edition Prometheans are getting Bestowments or similarly unique powers. If they are, then the Delphine's would be oracular visions, naturally.<br /> <br /> Those affected by a Delphine's Disquiet are convinced that she knows too much - they might be convinced she's spying on them or following them, or the suspicion may be more formless - and of course it's shaped by the nature of whatever secrets the affected possesses (people who share secrets may suspect one another of betraying them to the Promethean). A Delphine's Torment is madly ecstatic, unfiltered by wisdom or judgement, blurting out whatever words or actions cross her mind. In a Delphine's Wasteland, the air becomes stagnant and thick, with almost visible vapours around any gap in the ground - shadows seem deeper, while dreams and the corner of the eye seem to display flashes related to whatever decisions the individual is grappling with (though they provide confusuon rather than clarity).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T23:12:38-07:00","id":849619,"title":"","content":"I never really got that far in it, but I had the idea of a zombie based lineage.<br /> <br /> Easy enough to see obsession and the divine fire entering the picture when trying to create a cure for a zombie virus, or I suppose &quot;improving the disease&quot; if you work at Umbrella Corp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:18:02-07:00","id":943866,"title":"","content":"Always did want to add my own Supernatural Lineages for the fan games. Thankfully, 2E makes making a Lineage even easier since Mockery no longer exists as a concept and both Disquiet and Wasteland are generalized.<br /> <br /> Can't do that on a phone, but I do have ideas for a Princess-made one (a bodyguard and vizier for the True Heir) and a Leviathan's (a perfect priest). Geniuses, obviously, are &quot;all&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:09:25-07:00","id":943924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=943866#post943866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always did want to add my own Supernatural Lineages for the fan games. Thankfully, 2E makes making a Lineage even easier since Mockery no longer exists as a concept and both Disquiet and Wasteland are generalized.<br /> <br /> Can't do that on a phone, but I do have ideas for a Princess-made one (a bodyguard and vizier for the True Heir) and a Leviathan's (a perfect priest). Geniuses, obviously, are &amp;quot;all&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect priests would work just as well for Mummy. The only problem is making them distinct from the Osirans...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T22:00:47-07:00","id":944128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=943924#post943924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfect priests would work just as well for Mummy. The only problem is making them distinct from the Osirans...</div> </div> </div> </div>Make them natural traitors? Where Osirans get cold and detached, Promethean Priest get greedy and treacherous. It would put them into an interesting jam where they lose themselves to Torment, upset their master, and then have to either run or do something truly horrifying to atone in the eyes of their Master and the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T09:05:03-07:00","id":944354,"title":"","content":"I created the Talos Lineage for first edition a long time ago. I might need to update them to second edition at some point. I'd also started working on Geppetto Lineage, but given that others had been making Pinochio Lineages as well, I put that to the back burner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 08-05-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:59:42-07:00","id":946591,"title":"","content":"Fuck. Deleted it again.<br /> <br /> Here's what I managed to save from the Princess Promethean. Bestowment, when I get around to it, is about accessing the Akashic Record for information and postcognition, he's also an ex-Centimanus who Calcified the Solvent Alimbic; he wants to save other Freaks from themselves, and kept his ability to neutralize their powers so they stop long enough for them to listen. His Humor is Dreamstuff (giving him an acute sense of his own hidden urges and the web of fate that underlies the world), his Torment is recklessness and self-punishment, and his Wasteland is things losing their solidity and everything becoming uncertain-at extreme ends, creatures from the Dreamlands start unknowingly passing in and out of reality. Didn't decide on Disquiet, but I feel it manifests as a growing sense of him constantly judging you-and then rage at his &quot;hypocrisy&quot; when people inevitably realize he is flawed as they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Thevetat, The Mirror's Mendicant</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote</b>: <i>&quot;The true bearer of this body was starved and mummified alive to be free of karma. I am that which he left behind.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Devadatta was a monk. Devadatta was wise. And Devadatta was the cousin of Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, himself-but Devadatta did not have Gautama's humility or freedom from materialistic wants of fame. And as Gautama became famous and loved, Devadatta, who had spent his entire life as a monk and had awakened his spiritual power through long practice, he became jealous of the prince who had only known happiness until that fateful day where he saw a crippled man, and had found the enlightenment that eluded Devadatta anyway. Was he not many times his cousin's senior? Didn't he deserve to be rewarded for his faith and long suffering in search of inner peace? When the Buddha rejected his cousin's request for becoming the abbot of his monastery, recognizing the growing inner darkness and enslavement to personal wants, Devadatta snapped, and his jealousy made him a monster. Three times he tried to kill his cousin (once through assassins, once through a bolder, and a third by a monstrous elephant), and one time tried to fracture his own monastery into feuding factions to ensure that if he could not lead the others, then at least neither would Gautama. All failed, and eventually his karma grew so wicked and dark that it afflicted his current life, cursing him with a terrible and invariably fatal illness. But Devadatta was still wise, and saw that this was precisely what he deserved, to attack his cousin and teacher out of selfish spite. He sincerely begged for forgiveness, and the Buddha gave it-not nearly enough to purify his karma except through a thousand unhappy lives and more than one term in Naraka's deepest levels, but pure enough for him to be destined to find the elusive enlightenment at the end of his penance.<br /> <br /> The Created who names himself after the Theosophical Society's own moniker for the envious monk sees in himself something akin to his namesake's repentant lives-to him falls the duty of balancing the evil karma left behind by his demiurge. For Thevetat was meant to be wise and a monk by a girl who felt she deserved a guide to elusive enlightenment-and because mummified a holy man alive to do that, he is a monster who is painfully aware he is neither.<br /> <br /> Her name was Advika Desai, and the Crown's Custodian convinced her that her name (&quot;unique lord&quot;, if read as given name-surname) was a sign of prophecy. She was not always a vain girl, or even a spoiled one as so many would be True Heirs of the Kingdom of Light are said to be. She was born rich, but her parents walked the tightrope between spoiling and neglecting their daughter admirably, and given how she was always a genius (she was capable of reading college-level textbooks at ten), her future seemed bright. Then the Darkness came and ruined her father's IT business with a Darkspawn virus, and so she had to become a crank author, disguising what she knew to be complete bullshit about indigo children and alien angels in actual scientific terminology and intellect to create several relative bestsellers that made just enough to avoid starving or darker avenues of income. She found something that overcame her growing cynicism though, in the form of a modern Theosophist's theories on the spiritual development of humans, and how older, more racist versions of the philosophy-religion were actually compounding the problem. This agreed with what she knew of her family's Buddhism, and set her heart in political activism-and making her brain a fertile ground for Blossoming. But she was still so young-barely sixteen when the Light settled around her, and with the emotional development to match. Overwhelmed by her sudden thrust into an endless war against a force of entropy disincarnate, she clinged to the comforting whispers of the Queen of Mirrors as the only way to hold on to her sanity-things <i>would</i> get better, the Child Queen promised. You yourself will do it, with your wisdom, she said. In time, Advika came to believe she was the fated herald of Sanat Kumara, ruler of Shamballah the grandmaster of the Great White Brotherhood who had revealed the teachings of Theosophy to the world, the highest of the Lords of the Flame who inspired the image of Lucifer and his allies as angels of purest Light (unfairly, according to Theosophy, but perhaps an understandable error given what she later did). In time, she would become enlightened enough to communicate with the Ancient of Days consciously, and become the World Teacher who would guide the destined metamorphosis of humanity into a spiritually aware people with no need or fear of the Darkness. The Queen simply smiled and nodded, saying nothing but that a Hierophant is a kind of teacher, too.<br /> <br /> Five years after this revelation, in the wake of a most terrible battle, Advika became impatient. Yes, suffering brings enlightenment and all, but was enlightenment worth the continuing deaths of her friends? The Queen gave no answer but a familiar refrain; &quot;Hard Choices Means You Aren't Looking Hard Enough&quot;. She did not mean to patronize, and somehow did not-rather, Advika took it to heart. The problem, she decided, wasn't that she would have to bear tragedy after tragedy in hopes of one day finally opening her sight enough to behold brilliant Sanat. No, her problem, just as it was to the initial students of the Great White Brotherhood, was that she did not have an enlightened teacher of any kind to begin with-no living human had been yet so free of karma to follow the inner pathways to Shamballah within the heart, and still remain capable of speaking with their less enlightened species.<br /> <br /> Sokushinbutsu, the Japanese practice of living mummification, was a way of achieving the enlightenment so required tenfold. A monk nearing the end of his life would seal himself in a tomb and deny his own thirst while eating only a diet that would not feed any fat or muscle on his body, overcoming attachment in total so that his reincarnation would be that much more evolved. The successful ones died, of course-but if the mummy's soul could be brought <i>back...</i><br /> <br /> Of course, most sokushinbutsu were willing. Technically, the priest that Advika chose gave his consent to become her Light-reanimated mentor, but given how copious use of Speechio was involved, the &quot;willing&quot; part is dubious. Regardless, a much-loved prison missionary became the holy corpse his Princess needed, and in the caverns beneath a waterfall, his mummy was carefully impaled on three-faced <i>phurba </i>knives in image of the Crucifixion, and Advika's attendants sung holy songs as she bathed his body in the Light of her Charms, bidding the sun to impart its vitality to dead flesh, stopping only to dine on plain, raw rice and the purified water that splashed into the cave. Three days of prayer and magic later, in a flash of Pyros, the light congealed and settled across the seven major chakras, slowly fading into vital fluids as the corpse de-mummified just enough to live. Two tense, twitching minutes later, the Promethean that would one day be Thevetat opened once-dried eyes.<br /> <br /> And it was two days later that Advika faced the disappointment that all demiurges must-yes, the mummy could access knowledge beyond mortal ken easily, yes he had an insightful nature, but his mind was not that of the priest's; in fact, were it not for his ability to walk and talk, he might have well been an ignorant newborn. His Disquiet fed upon her frustrations and hidden horror at the realization she had effectively murdered an innocent man via torture for nothing, and she came to believe her creation was a foul spirit sent by the Brotherhood's enemies, the Lords of the Dark Face, to steal her teacher's body and deny her birthright at the last moment, and she conspired to kill the failed teacher and try again. But she wasn't misguided in her beliefs that her creation would have great spiritual power-in particular, his ability to draw on knowledge from beyond to protect himself from mystics that intended him harm. By the time she arrived with fire and spell, the mummy was long gone, having taken advantage of his Pyros-infused biology to survive the waterfall's rocks and heal from a passing thunderstorm. Also gone was her notes on his creation-he knew enough about the priest's life to known one must first know himself before teaching anything, and that seemed to be the best source. Coming to the end, as Disquiet set in, he came to agree with her-he <i>was</i> a dark spirit who was never human, but faced with his demiurge's selfishness, he also believed it was her own ignorance and attachment to a dream based on nothing more than her own hopes and belief to be what called him and forced him into a flesh that was not his; a mindless <i>tulpa </i>conjured from her own misconceptions and ignorance, only given true thought and the capacity to believe in his own existence when the priest's dead flesh gave him a brain to more fully believe in himself. In other words-he was the product of a complete failure and a stillborn dream, the congealed avatar of spiritual ignorance.<br /> <br /> He almost decided the most moral thing to do was to remove himself from the world right there and trouble it no more, but then his Elpis quickened, and in his first vision, revealed to him one final truth that Advika and her Queen had ignored-that darkness and spiritual ignorance is not the opposite of light and enlightenment, but its shell. By the existence of evil, is good defined and capable of evolving, the dance of Flux and Pyros. Was it really so hard to believe that a Promethean, born of the shell of humanity, incapable of of filling that shell with humanity-and then shedding it altogether? <br /> <br /> And so did Thevetat, then named for what he thought was the dragon that misled the people of Mu and indirectly begin the ancient war that destroyed the previous race of humans (and as he became more familiar with actual Buddhism and its myth, he has seen no reason to change it) begin his Pilgrimage, the path from the ignorance of an existence completely defined by the physical and into the New Dawn of a soul-and with it, the potential for true enlightenment and wisdom.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>While the priest whose body became him was a devout Buddhist, neither he nor the new occupant of his flesh are of Asian ethnicity-he was actually a black Californian who converted in high school and never looked back. Still, Thevetat is a devout Buddhist himself, and takes as much pains to appear as the traveling monk he so desperately wants to be-when he can get away with it, he wears the distinct ochre robes that hang loose from his right arm, revealing a set of scars that he's sustained both from the natural dangers of Promethean existence and from his occasional flirtations with self-flagellation (a Christian and Islamic practice rather than Buddhist, but he's a practical man when it comes to purification-he will do anything that seems to work). When he can't due to weather or evading human hunters, he favors sturdy traveler's clothes what hide his appearance as totally as he can manage, but in all he wears a bindi, a red dot in the center of the forehead. This isn't due to any fashion statement on his part (in truth, he thinks of the bindi as a feminine item-any male wearing it is cross-dressing, he feels, which is all fine and dandy for them but he isn't a fan of not dressing your preferred gender), but a philosophical one-the bindi symbolically represents the beginning of creation, which he technically is; when and if his creation is finished and he becomes Redeemed, he fully intends to get rid of it, as it is unneeded as a marker.<br /> <br /> When his Disfigurements are visible, Thevetat looks a great deal like an Osirian; his skin is pallid and leathery, his teeth are yellowed, and his nails black and uneven. He looks more <i>alive, </i>though-his eyes, the soft tissues of his mouth (including his lips), and his blood look exactly like they do when his disfigurements are hidden, giving people the uncomfortable sense that he is actually a living man wearing a skintight corpse. Here and there, cracks appear in his skin-when he charges an Alimbic, they release a gaseous blue light that drifts up to his head and forms a halo (though it takes him only a second's thought to cancel this, thankfully for his stealth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:18:59-07:00","id":947051,"title":"","content":"Man, I'd do anything for more on the Moreau, that sounds like a really cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:00:08-07:00","id":947330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=947051#post947051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I'd do anything for more on the Moreau, that sounds like a really cool idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. Working on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:20:47-07:00","id":947338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=947330#post947330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Noted. Working on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Though, just realized that the Pilgrimage poses a bit of a problem with them. You'd either have to de-emphasize it or give them the possibility of becoming animals, since The Island of Doctor Moreau makes it very clear that trying to turn animals into humans is a phenomenally bad idea. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm totally going to give these guys a nod in The Lightning Chronicle, since it wouldn't be a problem there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:06:15-07:00","id":948258,"title":"","content":"Frankenstein isn't exactly optimistic about the New Dawn either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:28:29-07:00","id":948271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=948258#post948258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankenstein isn't exactly optimistic about the New Dawn either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's what I've been saying. If we go down that route, though, we'll just get into another round of me ranting about Promethean getting Frankenstein wrong, and that's not helping anyone, let alone the topic of this thread. <br /> <br /> The problem with giving the &quot;Moreaus&quot; the standard &quot;become human&quot; New Dawn is that it means whatever mad scientist created them was essentially right, and it is actually possible and desirable to use science to forcibly alter animals into humans, and that's not really horror-y. Horror stories about mad science rarely end with the mad scientist looking things over and saying &quot;wow, that was a great idea!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:55:23-07:00","id":948327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=948271#post948271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with giving the &quot;Moreaus&quot; the standard &quot;become human&quot; New Dawn is that it means whatever mad scientist created them was essentially right, and it is actually possible and desirable to use science to forcibly alter animals into humans, and that's not really horror-y. Horror stories about mad science rarely end with the mad scientist looking things over and saying &quot;wow, that was a great idea!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not seeing a difference between that and any other Lineage. Of course I generally operate under the assumption that actually achieving the New Dawn is an incredibly rare occurrence even on the Promethean-scale, and the &quot;legacy&quot; of most Prometheans of any lineage is having left of a swath of Torment, Disquiet, and Wastelands in their wake, and perhaps cursed others to endure their fate (if they were fortunate enough not to make Pandorans instead).<br /> <br /> That said, I may leave it an open question if the Great Work is even possible for the Moreau, as is the case with the Extemporae in the 2E core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T21:34:14-07:00","id":948348,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the idea of a &quot;wood-elemental&quot; themed Lineage. But I'm failing to come up with anything rooted in Chinese lore or literature to base them on. Instead, I'm imagining corpses reanimated by azoth-charged plant (or fungal) growth. <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/RsTDUDG.png\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the type of thing I'm thinking of as seen on NBC's Hannibal (disturbing image warning!)</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of calling them the Haoma (named for both legendary plant and Zoroastrian divinity they claim as Demiurge).<br /> <br /> Should their humour just be &quot;sap&quot; in balance with the Unfleshed having &quot;oil&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-11-2016, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T21:41:39-07:00","id":948352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=948327#post948327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still not seeing a difference between that and any other Lineage. Of course I generally operate under the assumption that actually achieving the New Dawn is an incredibly rare occurrence even on the Promethean-scale, and the &amp;quot;legacy&amp;quot; of most Prometheans of any lineage is having left of a swath of Torment, Disquiet, and Wastelands in their wake, and perhaps cursed others to endure their fate (if they were fortunate enough not to make Pandorans instead).<br /> <br /> That said, I may leave it an open question if the Great Work is even possible for the Moreau, as is the case with the Extemporae in the 2E core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I guess that works. It's all a moot point for purposes of The Lightning Chronicle anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:54:03-07:00","id":955294,"title":"","content":"An Integrator has pulled off an elaborate tricks years in the making, and now has a piece of Infrastructure originally designed for producing new Angels. She knows that the Machine that created her is flawed, that it cannot be redeemed... but perhaps she can take its place? The obsession to create grows burns in her mechanical heart as she pores over the occult matrices used to create Covers out of thin air, but she wants to refine the process further, to create new life and cement her role as a replacement demiurge in the universe. The factory explodes in a shower of lightning and its master is immediately consumed by the blaze... but not before Aether was injected into the veins of the vat-grown body at its core. The new life stumbles out of the wreckage, their pale skin covered in tattoos of sacred mathematical formulae, and they begin a long Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> What does it mean to be a Cover with no true identity behind it, a spy without a cause or an enemy? The new life does not know, but they dream of gears and angels when they sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:58:03-07:00","id":955527,"title":"","content":"So the element is aether? The humour could be breath, perhaps. Or perhaps a &quot;Vital Humour&quot; - which I usually use for a Promethean made by a vampire, but in this case could refer to the impulses that run through brain and nerves. Disquiet could covey a sense of oppression - that the Promethean controls everything and is manipulating your life to some end. Wasteland could fray time and space, though I'm not sure how to manifest that. Torment could manifest as extreme single mindedness - like an angel - towards whatever the Promethean was doing at the time the Torment took hold, whether or not it makes sense for it to be a continuous course of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:51:09-07:00","id":955580,"title":"","content":"So, I've been unable to stop considering the idea of an Extempore lineage inspired by Swamp-Thing and Man-Thing, most of whom tend to arise either when a Tammuz tries its generative rite in a rainforest or swamp and chance interferes, or an Ulgan tries to breathe life into a wooden sculpture.<br /> <br /> Element is Wood (a cocktail of Earth, Water and Plant) and Humor is Sap.<br /> <br /> Their disfigurement is that they're clearly a &quot;muck encrusted mockery of a man&quot; - they're corpses that have been largely consumed by vegetable elements, with things like moss or fungus covering their flesh, roots growing out of their skin, or even just being a collection of roots filled with moss in the shape of a human.<br /> <br /> Haven't gotten much further into developing it - can't think of a decent name for them, for starters - but I was wondering if, by the &quot;rules&quot; of Promethean's setting, such a thing would be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T22:18:18-07:00","id":958610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=946591#post946591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Thevetat, The Mirror's Mendicant</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Finally got back to this:<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Thevetat often comes off as wiser than he feels he has a right to be-he's never truly gotten over the fact that his intended purpose was a colossal failure, and he's convinced himself that until he has completed the Magnum Opus, his insights will be fundamentally tainted by the karma that gave birth to him. A long time ago, he blamed himself for existing, and after a particularly misguided decision on his part, came to believe he did not deserve humanity because of it-and in one of the most mixed blessings in the history of the Divine Fire, had also come to realize he had a right to exist. Seduced by Flux, Thevetat attempted to redefine himself as an Asura, one of the semi-divine demons born of people defined in their previous life by noble but self-destructive passions, especially righteous anger and the desire to change the world by force alone. This made him, if anything, even more miserable over time-his very humour wants him to be a teacher, and Asuras are monstrous warriors by nature and purpose. Nobody wants to be allies with such awful beings, let alone friends-but the actual nature of the Mirror's Mendicant indirectly saved him, when a Radiant Noble was drawn to the strange, surreal anomalies of Light surrounding his self-made monastery. She taught him that what he was doing wasn't the hope for a rebirth he claimed, but a habit he picked up to fill the hole his despair left behind-and then taught him to hope again, even through the growing Disquiet. Coming to his senses, Thevetat shed his Flux in a roar of Tin to understand what <i>real </i>righteous anger was, and from there found his way back to the path. He's realized the real curse of the Promethean condition is the simple fact that they do not <i>have </i>any personal karma-every curse on his existence is the repayment for the crimes of other creatures, and the tragedy is that he is to blame for none of it. By all rights, he should be able to happily continue the Saturnine Night indefinitely, but the very nature of the Created is an injustice forever inflicted on them, a barrier to Nirvana one that can never be rectified except by forcing himself into the wheel of reincarnation to ascend or fail on his own merits. This revelation hasn't made him bitter, though-he has also realized it isn't humanity's fault he brings out the worst in them either, it's only his demiurge's hubris and abuse of the natural order (this <i>is </i>one of the reasons he finds Theosophy a ridiculous philosophy, though).<br /> <br /> These days, the rage Thevetat once felt has been expended and calmed, and he's mostly a pacifist-in fact, the one thing he Calcified from Stannum was his ability to instantly nonlethally defeat someone suffering from Disquiet. Centimani and amoral walkers of the Pilgrimage quickly discover both his sordid past and the fact he is not an idiot, however-he Calcified the Disruption Alimbic from the Flux Transmutations as well, and in fact did so for the purpose of saving Centimani from themselves; it's his personal mission in life to turn at least one Freak away from the path that leads nowhere, and he is fully aware that most would rather eat him than stand still long enough for him to attack their self-justification, so he quite intentionally parlayed with Flux permanently in order to force the issue (thankfully for him, Flux is entropic, not evil-there is no physical law which states this is doomed to failure). He's also developed the quirk of giving funeral rites to any Pandorans he or the throngs he has allied himself with have killed; he's come to believe the reason they can't redefine themselves as Prometheans is that they actually do have personal karma, because they have souls-of <i>pretas, </i>the hungry ghosts driven by instinct. Yes, said pretas likely deserved such a miserable incarnation, but they are still people-and this fate is ultimately temporary. Once they are no longer a threat, he feels, it's better to at least recognize that was a person with hopes and dreams once.<br /> <br /> <b>Refinement: </b>Cuprum. Having worked out his self-hate through Stannum, understood his nature through Plumbum, and having realized the nature of negative karma through Cobalus (actually his personal favorite, as it allowed him to skip the messy process of therapy to impart inner peace directly), Thevetat has dedicated himself to learning what an actual teacher is, and from there immerse himself in the true natural order of things-being a true stranger to it, he needs to learn harmony academically as well as intrinsically before he can be one with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Lineage: </b>None, as of yet. While Thevetat is sure he's not an Extempore (he has Elpis visions), there's two reasons he has not made progeny, yet. The first is a religious conflict-if he fails, in his view, he's condemning at least one <i>preta </i>to an even more miserable existence for a period, likely more, and if he succeeds, then there's another living violation of karma in the world, one that echoes no human but humanity itself, increasing his progeny's misery tenfold. The other is a more substantial moral one-he's almost certain his generative preparation would involve mummifying another person alive, or something similar. Actually doing that himself is out of the question, and he's been so sure his act of <i>multiplicato </i>will be successful teaching of another Promethean he hasn't bothered scrounging the world for a suitable corpse. Still, if he is convinced there's a less horrifying way of making a perfect student and he's convinced there is no other way, he has no particular objections to the generative act-he knows the New Dawn is possible for his progeny, and again, <i>pretas </i>don't end up that way without deserving it.<br /> <br /> <b>Humour: </b>Dreamstuff. Somewhere between driven ectoplasm and intellectual phlegm lies Thevetat's personality core. He is naturally introspective and calmly self-aware about his motivations, and easily turns that towards empathic understanding of others-he's not always <i>good </i>at reading others, but he's naturally curious about the inner lives of other individuals and very aware of the web of subconscious drives, social influences, and fate that drives humanity and himself. Normally he is at peace with this, but when Torment strikes, he becomes painfully aware of how separate he is from the normal, and usually <i>functional, </i>mass of humanity. He feels alienated and ignored, and he blames his darker personality traits for everything that has gone wrong in his life, leading to spectacularly self-destructive acts in misguided attempts to expurgate the flaws in his spirit (and naturally, it is <i>never enough, </i>only ending his penance when his mind clears and he realizes how pointless his actions have been). His associated element is illumination-he must sleep in an area so well-lit there is no darkness but shadows to regain Pyros in his sleep. Ironically, this also means he leads an often nocturnal existence, as that is easiest to do during the day.<br /> <br /> <b>Bestowment: </b>Akashic Records. By meditating for five turns, Thevetat may spend one Pyros roll Intelligence + Resolve. For every success, his player may ask the Storyteller one question about the past, present, or immediate (within two days) future of a sentient person, a place, or an item he has encountered or had described accurately to him (though the later case inflicts a -2 dice penalty) that can be answered in seven words or less. The Storyteller must answer to the best of their ability-if they cannot phrase it in proper terms, the question is not wasted. While Thevetat can use this Bestowment on something multiple times, this comes at a cost-every reading he uses on a specific thing besides the first inflicts a cumulative -1 penalty to his next Torment roll, as being so close to true karma reminds him of how far he is from mortality.<br /> <br /> <b>Disquiet: </b>Thevetat's Disquiet is unique, as it actually inflicts admiration-at first. Anyone who pays attention quickly realizes it's not a healthy admiration either, the vicvtims always compare him favorably to themselves-he's more handsome, more wise, more honest, and so on-and he always seems to be judging them for their repeated failures to live up to his ideal. At first, people under the influence just ignore him to avoid their own growing shame and self-loathing, but as Disquiet progresses to its later stages, its victims gradually have a revelation that Thevetat is not as perfect as he seems-and it <i>infuriates </i>them, to realize they have been shamed and spat on by a hypocrite and a liar. By the time the lynch mobs come, they're far too morally outraged at his &quot;deception&quot; to hear his words of pleading as anything but more baldfaced lies pretending to be righteousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Wasteland: </b>The Divine Fire of dreamstuff changes the relationship between what is real and what is imaginary-mirages become common, objects lose solidity, and the inhabitants of Thevetat's Wasteland become prone to delusions and mood swings as what was previously subconscious becomes conscious and vice versa. As it worsens, improbable and unlikely events, especially those relating to superstitions (step on a crack, break your mother's back) become a fact of life, and bits of the Dreamlands flicker in and out of the waking world. Unlike most Wastelands, the inhabitants don't become grouchy or violent, just weird-the Light doesn't like hurting people. Unfortunately, the Dreamlands that manifest are those that correspond to the jealousy and desperation Thevetat feels-in other words, places where Amanojaku lair and plot. At extreme ends, Gates of Polished Horn may spontaneously form from random detritus in the area, ready to serve as portals for the eager invaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-27-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}